    "intro_html":  "Kabsa is the national rice dish of Saudi Arabia, and it is built the smart way: the meat cooks first, then the rice cooks in that same spiced broth so nothing gets wasted. Cinnamon, cardamom, cloves, and coriander do the work, and toasted almonds and golden raisins go on top at the end. Our turkey version runs \u003cstrong\u003e564 calories and 42 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$6.40\u003c/strong\u003e a bowl (at everyday cost).",
